 ## Open questions
 
 The records leave these points undecided. Each side is stated as its record holds it; none is settled until the user answers.
 
-- **Approval of final terms.** The architecture record, the offer-and-reservation interface, the multi-lender exclusion record and the offer selection say publication is standing acceptance and reservation creates the canonical loan with no second lender approval; the loan-terms responsibility, the terms interface and the origination flow say both roles explicitly approve the same candidate and the second matching approval commits it. Neither is settled.
-- **Fee when no signed tier qualifies.** The fee interface's payload says to select the 200 satoshis-per-virtual-byte tier, record CPFP eligibility and alert for a separate manual fee approval, as do two ticket resolutions; the same interface's tier-selection action says to fail closed and select nothing. Neither is settled.
-- **Number of terminal packages.** One sentence of the package-construction responsibility speaks of a twelve-package terminal phase, while its own construction statement, the manifest interface and the Bitcoin state records specify six borrower-recovery, six lender-recovery and six borrower long-stop variants, eighteen in all. Neither count is settled.
